    "english":  "In the withered summer forest where the glorious flame-lilies have burnt away,\nwhere no patch of shade shelters the stony trails,\nthe hungry tigress waits in the narrow defile beside the rocks,\nhoping to ambush lonely travelers to feed her cubs in the dark evening.\nHow will my gentle girl endure that fearful path on foot?\nShe whose eyes would moisten with tears and whose breath would catch in deep sighs\nif I merely loosened my embrace for fear of pressing\nher tender, budding breasts too firmly against my chestΓÇö\nhow can her delicate feet tread those burning stones in the perilous wild?",
